# Twenty-One Medical — redirects
# Applies to the twentyonemedical.com Netlify site
# (repo GrowWithAmeliorateLLC/twenty-one-medical, published from the repo root).
# Targets are root-relative. First match wins, so order matters.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THERE ARE TWO SLUG FAMILIES
#
# The old WordPress site exposed the same services under two naming schemes:
#
#   long  — /medical-urgent-care, /family-medicine-clinic, ...
#           these were the links in the old homepage BODY
#   short — /urgent-care, /family-medicine, ...
#           these are what sitemap.xml lists, i.e. what Google indexed
#
# The first version of this file only covered the long family, because it was
# built by crawling the old homepage's links. Verified against
# twentyonemedical.com/sitemap.xml on 10/18/2026: 13 of the 14 indexed URLs
# had no rule. Both families are now covered.
#
# Everything lands at the TOP of the destination page, with no #fragment, on
# purpose. Someone arriving from an "urgent care" search needs to read the
# primary-care framing and the "not an emergency facility" note before
# anything else. Do not add fragments to the clinical-care rules.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Clinical: family medicine --------------------------------------------
/family-medicine              /clinical-care/         301!
/family-medicine/             /clinical-care/         301!
/family-medicine-clinic       /clinical-care/         301!
/family-medicine-clinic/      /clinical-care/         301!

# --- Clinical: same-day -----------------------------------------------------
# The practice is NOT licensed as an urgent care. These old URLs carry
# rankings and must keep resolving, but the phrase never reappears in any
# destination page's copy. Do not create a new URL containing it.
/urgent-care                  /clinical-care/         301!
/urgent-care/                 /clinical-care/         301!
/medical-urgent-care          /clinical-care/         301!
/medical-urgent-care/         /clinical-care/         301!

# --- Clinical: orthopedics --------------------------------------------------
/orthopedics                  /clinical-care/         301!
/orthopedics/                 /clinical-care/         301!
/orthopedic-sports-medicine   /clinical-care/         301!
/orthopedic-sports-medicine/  /clinical-care/         301!

# --- Weight loss ------------------------------------------------------------
/weight-loss                  /medical-weight-loss/   301!
/weight-loss/                 /medical-weight-loss/   301!
/weight-loss-solutions        /medical-weight-loss/   301!
/weight-loss-solutions/       /medical-weight-loss/   301!

# --- Aesthetics: everything folds into the laser hub ------------------------
# /laser-hair-removal was live and is the strongest-performing service URL on
# the old site. The hub covers hair removal first and by name. Revisit if
# rankings dip after launch.
/laser-hair-removal           /laser-treatments/      301!
/laser-hair-removal/          /laser-treatments/      301!
/skin-rejuvenation            /laser-treatments/      301!
/skin-rejuvenation/           /laser-treatments/      301!

# EmSculpt NEO, Botox and hair restoration are out of the current build scope.
# Their old URLs 404 today, so they point at the laser hub until those pages
# exist rather than staying dead. EmSculpt NEO is the body-contouring device
# named on the old site — this file is where that was first recorded.
/emsculpt-neo                 /laser-treatments/      301!
/emsculpt-neo/                /laser-treatments/      301!
/botox                        /laser-treatments/      301!
/botox/                       /laser-treatments/      301!
/botox-treatments             /laser-treatments/      301!
/botox-treatments/            /laser-treatments/      301!

# /hair-restoration — slug NOT verified against the old site and NOT in the
# sitemap. Do not enable until confirmed; a wrong 301 hides the problem
# instead of fixing it.
# /hair-restoration           /laser-treatments/      301!

# --- Services overview ------------------------------------------------------
# The new build has no single services hub. The homepage lists every program,
# so that is the honest destination.
/services                     /                       301!
/services/                    /                       301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRAILING-SLASH NORMALISATION
#
# netlify.toml sets pretty_urls = false, which switches off Netlify's
# automatic directory trailing-slash redirect. Without the rules below,
# /about would not resolve to /about/ and six indexed URLs whose names did
# NOT change would still 404 at cutover. These are the easiest rules to
# forget precisely because the slug looks already-correct.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/about                        /about/                 301!
/contact                      /contact/               301!
/book-online                  /book-online/           301!
/iv-therapy                   /iv-therapy/            301!
/hormone-replacement-therapy  /hormone-replacement-therapy/  301!
/peptide-therapy              /peptide-therapy/       301!

